baseline.response:
Looking at your code, I can see exactly what happened:

## Problem 1: The 11k skipped sends

```handlebars
{{#ifGte daysSinceLastOrder 90}}
```

**This is the culprit.** In Iterable, comparison helpers (`#ifGte`, `#ifGt`, `#ifLte`, `#ifLt`) **fail the entire send** if the field is null, undefined, or missing. Those 11k people likely have no `daysSinceLastOrder` value — maybe they never ordered, or the data sync missed them.

## Problem 2: Broken links

```handlebars
<a href="{{returnUrl}}?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">
```

If `returnUrl` is null/empty, this becomes `href="?utm_source=..."` which is broken. For users who did get the email but have missing/null `returnUrl`, the link is dead.

---

## The fix

```handlebars
{{#if daysSinceLastOrder}}
  {{#ifGte daysSinceLastOrder 90}}
    {{!-- Lapsed customers (90+ days) --}}
    <p>It's been a while, {{defaultIfEmpty firstName "there"}}! Here's 20% off.</p>
    {{#if returnUrl}}
      <a href="{{returnUrl}}?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
    {{else}}
      <a href="https://yoursite.com/shop?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
    {{/if}}
  {{else}}
    {{!-- Recent customers --}}
    <p>Thanks for being a regular, {{defaultIfEmpty firstName "there"}}.</p>
    {{#if returnUrl}}
      <a href="{{returnUrl}}?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Continue shopping</a>
    {{/if}}
  {{/ifGte}}
{{else}}
  {{!-- No order history - treat as new/prospect --}}
  <p>Ready to try us? Here's 20% off your first order.</p>
  <a href="https://yoursite.com/shop?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback_new">Shop now</a>
{{/if}}
```

**What changed:**
1. **Outer `{{#if daysSinceLastOrder}}`** — proves the field exists before any comparison runs, preventing send skips
2. **`{{#if returnUrl}}`** guards around every link — uses a fallback URL when `returnUrl` is missing
3. **`defaultIfEmpty firstName "there"`** — handles missing first names gracefully
4. Added an `{{else}}` for users with no order history (your 11k skipped sends)

**Replace `https://yoursite.com/shop` with your actual fallback URL.**

---

## Verify before resending

Test in **Content → Templates → Preview with data**:
- Load a real user, then manually edit their data to test:
  - A user with `daysSinceLastOrder: null` (simulates no order history)
  - A user with `daysSinceLastOrder: 150` and `returnUrl: null` (simulates broken link scenario)
  - A user with `daysSinceLastOrder: 30` (recent customer path)

This will catch both issues before you send again.

